{"lines":[{"x":0.20987654236543979,"c":1,"w":0.053497943878173859,"t":"Test 4","h":0.013250883392226132,"y":0.10895170803527432},{"x":0.20987654421052079,"w":0.26954732259114589,"c":1,"y":0.14958775026742666,"t":"READING PASSAGE 3","h":0.014723203769140158},{"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading","x":0.20973868848108129,"c":1,"w":0.72247522989908863,"y":0.18162150815262923,"h":0.020094829959217964},{"h":0.016221728285574999,"t":"Passage 3 below.","y":0.19601979205286213,"w":0.14474586486816404,"x":0.20952285287663097,"c":1},{"x":0.20975226725476129,"y":0.22802313139632069,"h":0.017616184355934594,"c":1,"w":0.7142129516601563,"t":"Chelsea Rochman, an ecologist at the University of California, Davis, has been trying to answer"},{"h":0.01914370776065244,"t":"a dismal question: Is everything terrible, or are things just very, very bad?","y":0.24320356320440295,"c":1,"w":0.55173558553059898,"x":0.20766328021599956},{"c":1,"y":0.27401776769434905,"h":0.017090043695851986,"t":"Rochman is a member of the National Center for Ecological Analysis and Synthesis's","x":0.20973057018409672,"w":0.63402343750000001},{"y":0.2886468006069367,"x":0.2077062452048862,"t":"marine-debris working group, a collection of scientists who study, among other things, the","w":0.67308720906575514,"h":0.018265529852733442,"c":1},{"w":0.69570826212565107,"h":0.018701027644396739,"c":1,"x":0.20974661779547762,"y":0.30499335261619476,"t":"growing problem of marine debris, also known as ocean trash. Plenty of studies have sounded"},{"w":0.71027872721354168,"h":0.021223452402930332,"c":1,"x":0.20559890625690078,"t":"alarm bells about the state of marine debris; in a recent paper published in the journal Ecology,","y":0.3189709638893321},{"y":0.33506692568835383,"h":0.02067416520225418,"c":1,"x":0.2056047347589644,"t":"Rochman and her colleagues set out to determine how many of those perceived risks are real.","w":0.69785685221354177},{"h":0.019409821086834089,"t":"Often, Rochman says, scientists will end a paper by speculating about the broader impacts of","y":0.366158020326666,"w":0.69366811116536453,"c":1,"x":0.20767702858290857},{"h":0.02004771687537954,"x":0.20563281307336506,"c":1,"t":"what they've found. For example, a study could show that certain seabirds eat plastic bags, and","w":0.70806086222330733,"y":0.38173632915807088},{"x":0.2077137421628828,"h":0.017807419083845755,"y":0.39774181256266261,"c":1,"w":0.72038136800130204,"t":"go on to warn that whole bird populations are at risk of dying out. 'But the truth was that nobody"},{"x":0.20564810282694973,"y":0.41268192505152967,"w":0.67096481323242196,"h":0.0190505487197139,"c":1,"t":"had yet tested those perceived threats,' Rochman says.iThere wasn't a lot of information.?"},{"h":0.015674952202607062,"y":0.44440074291084419,"c":1,"x":0.20773405427935376,"t":"Rochman and her colleagues examined more than a hundred papers on the impacts of marine","w":0.69151570638020832},{"y":0.45822003879605555,"t":"debris that were published through 2013. Within each paper, they asked what threats scientists","x":0.20353986036410571,"h":0.020392574045206002,"w":0.70198343912760408,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"had studied - 366 perceived threats in all - and what they'd actually found.","x":0.20370371127852668,"w":0.55967076619466138,"y":0.47526501739877658,"h":0.016014052504504606},{"y":0.50420511597446349,"c":1,"x":0.20559301216385278,"h":0.019016647788183683,"w":0.70402369181315105,"t":"In 83 percent of cases, the perceived dangers of ocean trash were proven true. In the remaining"},{"c":1,"x":0.20362034506541382,"y":0.52067922756289964,"h":0.017838139416050947,"t":"cases, the working group found the studies had weaknesses in design and content which affected","w":0.7182669067382812},{"w":0.66903442382812484,"t":"the validity of their conclusions - they lacked a control group, for example, or used faulty","h":0.019440198253546259,"c":1,"y":0.53574676453032022,"x":0.20353607598739784},{"c":1,"y":0.55171525911937569,"t":"statistics.","x":0.20551680022434415,"h":0.01102204541856755,"w":0.072815043131510437},{"y":0.58121619016739123,"x":0.20351882522765086,"c":1,"w":0.69993886311848963,"h":0.020809483612383994,"t":"Strikingly, Rochman says, only one well-designed study failed to find the effect it was looking"},{"y":0.59732751880917345,"h":0.019345203754618234,"t":"for, an investigation of mussels ingesting microscopic plastic bits. The plastic moved from the","w":0.70188390096028641,"c":1,"x":0.20151239579682434},{"t":"mussels' stomachs to their bloodstreams, scientists found, and stayed there for weeks - but didn't","w":0.72033330281575525,"x":0.20568287156749154,"h":0.016355440389141163,"c":1,"y":0.61312738199018024},{"t":"seem to stress out the shellfish.","h":0.015106624652696299,"c":1,"y":0.62741522129746474,"w":0.23301025390624999,"x":0.20351570702610303},{"x":0.20354093545526297,"y":0.65822103517400654,"t":"While mussels may be fine eating trash, though, the analysis also gave a clearer picture of the","w":0.69575851440429681,"h":0.019964678689082693,"c":1},{"w":0.32942019144694007,"y":0.67453384854047083,"c":1,"x":0.20361662263394759,"h":0.014471845997517163,"t":"many ways that ocean debris is bothersome."},{"x":0.20559228343044736,"h":0.01988649199792436,"c":1,"t":"Within the studies they looked at, most of the proven threats came from plastic debris, rather than","y":0.70318880155581953,"w":0.72253260294596344},{"h":0.019048973865306906,"c":1,"t":"other materials like metal or wood. Most of the dangers also involved large pieces of debris -","w":0.69369878133138019,"y":0.71902887022918371,"x":0.20356772562897996},{"t":"animals getting entangled in trash, for example, or eating it and severely injuring themselves.","x":0.20154922841943326,"y":0.73534180844951225,"w":0.69361852010091152,"h":0.018154015108609478,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"But a lot of ocean debris is 'microplastic', or pieces smaller than five millimeters. These may","x":0.20357774534796685,"y":0.76551165148610378,"w":0.68955032348632805,"h":0.01857697696932914},{"c":1,"x":0.20355935045422824,"y":0.78162377159543339,"t":"be ingredients used in cosmetics and toiletries, fibers shed by synthetic clothing in the wash, or","h":0.018189108975503743,"w":0.70600550333658851},{"x":0.20355148463278228,"y":0.79618190939826439,"w":0.69576385498046878,"h":0.019112325248224038,"t":"eroded remnants of larger debris. Compared to the number of studies investigating large-scale","c":1},{"y":0.81234096113502618,"w":0.71417292277018229,"h":0.017008655624479507,"x":0.20358508883517931,"c":1,"t":"debris, Rochman's group found little research on the effects of these tiny bits.iThere are a lot of"},{"t":"open questions still for microplastic,' Rochman says, though she notes that more papers on the","y":0.82559706247765907,"h":0.022202625431918976,"w":0.70201721191406252,"c":1,"x":0.20145599684345863},{"c":1,"y":0.84210417021818185,"t":"subject have been published since 2013, the cutoff point for the group's analysis.","w":0.60121724446614588,"x":0.19940094289481636,"h":0.021120060178219768},{"t":"90","w":0.024691357612609877,"h":0.013081395583944722,"y":0.86482558121238806,"x":0.19958847746941524,"c":1}],"h":3395,"w":2400}